_:c14n20 sh:class owl:Axiom ;
	sh:description "A list of mapping objects (also known as “mapping records”).\nMapping objects within such a list are always independent of each other and, therefore, MUST be interpreted in isolation. This means, for example, that if a list contains a mapping between A and B, and a mapping between A and C, the only possible interpretation is that A is mapped independently to B and to C – NOT that A is mapped to some combination of B and C.\nThat mappings must be interpreted in isolation does not preclude drawing inferences from several mappings, as long as each mapping is always interpreted on its own." ;
	sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
	sh:order 2 ;
	sh:path sssom:mappings .
